# =============================================================================
# GIT IGNORE FILE
# Purpose: Tells Git which files/folders to NEVER track or commit.
# Why it exists: Keeps the repository clean, small, and free of machine-
# specific or auto-generated files that don't belong in version history.
# =============================================================================

# Dependency folders — these are auto-downloaded by npm/pip and can contain
# tens of thousands of files. They're rebuilt from package.json/requirements.txt,
# so tracking them in Git is unnecessary and would bloat the repo massively.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build output — generated automatically when we compile/bundle the project.
# Never hand-edited, always regenerated, so no reason to track it.
dist/
build/

# Environment variable files — these WILL eventually hold configuration
# values. Even though this project won't use secret API keys, this is a
# professional safety habit: NEVER let environment files enter Git history,
# ever, on any project, even if they seem harmless today.
.env
.env.local

# Editor/IDE-specific settings — these are personal to each developer's
# machine (font size, extensions, etc.) and would create noisy, irrelevant
# changes if tracked.
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS-generated junk files — Windows and Mac automatically create tiny hidden
# files in folders (like thumbnail caches). These have nothing to do with
# our project and clutter the repo if tracked.
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Log files — generated automatically while the app runs, constantly
# changing, and not useful as permanent project history.
*.log